# The PDA writing zone's key strip (report 041, 042) in the terminal (CLI): the terminal asks for text input as it does
# for the on-screen keyboard, so the band shows (the strip on top of the writing boxes; the terminal leaves its rows free
# as for the keyboard). Ctrl tapped is armed (lit) for the next key; a "c" written in the letters box then sends Ctrl+C
# (the fake shell echoes ^C and a new prompt) and Ctrl goes off; a pound sign (the extended prefix, then an l) reaches
# the terminal as UTF-8 text (its own font draws it). The strip's keyboard key (report 042) puts the on-screen keyboard
# in the writing boxes' place (vkb auto: the exact keyboard, a sudo password): s, u and Enter reach the terminal as
# keys; the key again brings the writing boxes back. Goldens at both sizes.
title zone strip
sizes 480x640 480x800
profile pda
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
expect_zone hidden
launch CLI
ptyout "user@pda:~$ "
wait 300
expect_zone shown
expect_vkb zone
zonekey Ctrl
shot zone_strip_ctrl
stroke letters 117,55 110,46 102,38 92,32 81,30 69,31 59,34 49,42 44,55 41,67 40,78 41,89 45,101 50,111 58,120 68,127 80,130 91,127 101,120 110,110 115,103
shot zone_strip_ctrl_c
stroke letters 60,30 145,115
stroke letters 60,30 60,130 121,130
shot zone_strip_pound
zonekey Kbd
expect_zone keys
expect_vkb auto
shot zone_strip_keys
tapkey s
tapkey u
tapkey ENTER
ptylog zone_strip_pty
shot zone_strip_typed
zonekey Kbd
expect_zone writing
expect_vkb zone
